\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{The simplicial momentum grid}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{Let #{n\ge1}, #{N_1,\ldots,N_n\ge3}, and let
#{R=\prod_{j=1}^n\mathbb Z/N_j\mathbb Z} be the character labels
of \ref{fdip-000S}. Their real momenta have coordinates
#{p_j=2\pi r_j/N_j}. Write #{e_j} for the #{j}-th unit
step. For #{r\in R} and a permutation #{\pi} of the axes,
the \newvocab{grid simplex} #{\sigma_{r,\pi}} has ordered vertices
##{v_0=r,\qquad v_i=r+\sum_{h=1}^ie_{\pi(h)}
\quad(1\le i\le n).}
Kuhn gives these partial sums for a cube
\citet{p. 520, Lemma 1 and Corollary}{kuhn1960combinatorial}.
Its simplex faces are the subsets of these vertices. Over an ordered
field #{k}, a point of this simplex has weights
#{\lambda_i\ge0} with #{\sum_i\lambda_i=1}. For the periodic grid, glue neighboring cube faces, including
the two faces across each seam, by identifying their common
vertex weights. For #{f:R\to k^n} the \newvocab{interpolated map}
has value #{\tilde f=\sum_i\lambda_i f(v_i)}.}
